      <h2 id="virt-setting-policy-attributes_virt-schedule-vms" class="group scroll-mt-20">Setting a policy attribute and CPU feature<a href="#virt-setting-policy-attributes_virt-schedule-vms" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can set a policy attribute and CPU feature for each virtual machine (VM) to ensure that it is scheduled on a node according to policy and feature. The CPU feature that you set is verified to ensure that it is supported by the host CPU or emulated by the hypervisor.</p>
